From: CBOC-Vita <cboc-vita@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] 1.3: a scissor-mask rebuild the depth/stencil surface already holds is not drawn (vglSetMaskKeep, MASK_KEEP)

MSC_VGX_VGL_MASKKEEP (default on; the Galaxy port's vitaGL 0018 MASK_KEEP, run on by default on its console; written again from the description):
update_scissor_test draws the mask from nothing (a full-target quad that clears the bit and the region quad that sets it) at every framebuffer-object
scene start, every return to the display and every scissor or attribute restore. The quads are deterministic, so each depth/stencil surface keeps a
record of the mask it holds and a rebuild equal to the record is not drawn. Records are dropped for new surface memory, a scene that does not load or
does not store the surface, a clear that writes stencil, and table overflow. vglSetMaskKeep(GL_FALSE) (the library default) draws every rebuild.
Host test: renderer/tests/run_vitagl_maskkeep_test.sh.

--- a/source/gxm.c
+++ b/source/gxm.c
@@ -561,6 +561,7 @@ GLboolean init_depth_stencil_buffer_ms(uint32_t w, uint32_t h, SceGxmDepthStenci
 	// Initializing mask update bit to 1
 	vgl_memset(depth_buffer, 0x80, 4 * depth_stencil_samples);
 #endif
+	vgl_mk_forget(depth_buffer); // 1.3 MASK_KEEP (tests.c): new memory, whatever an old surface at this address held
 #endif
 
 	// Allocating stencil surface
@@ -814,6 +815,8 @@ GLboolean scene_reset(void) {
 
 		if (rt_time)
 			rt_t2 = vgl_rt_now();
+		// 1.3 MASK_KEEP (tests.c): what the scene's depth/stencil surface brings in, with the load and store modes it begun with
+		vgl_mk_scene_begin(is_rendering_display ? &gxm_depth_stencil_surface : active_write_fb->depthbuffer_ptr);
 		// RT: a surface that was not loaded holds the background mask (0): rebuild the mask as every framebuffer object scene does
 		if (rt_applied & VGL_RT_NOLOAD) {
 			dirty_scissor_state = GL_TRUE;
--- a/source/misc.c
+++ b/source/misc.c
@@ -814,12 +814,16 @@ void glClear(GLbitfield mask) {
 		vgl_lc_in_clear = GL_FALSE;
 		if (!ok)
 			return; // 1.2: no scene could be started: the clear is skipped
+		if (mask & GL_STENCIL_BUFFER_BIT)
+			vgl_mk_touch(); // 1.3 MASK_KEEP (tests.c): the mask is not assumed to survive a stencil clear
 		lc_clear(mask);
 		return;
 	}
 #endif
 	if (!scene_reset())
 		return; // 1.2: no scene could be started: the clear is skipped
+	if (mask & GL_STENCIL_BUFFER_BIT)
+		vgl_mk_touch(); // 1.3 MASK_KEEP (tests.c): the mask is not assumed to survive a stencil clear
 
 	// Invalidating viewport and culling
 	invalidate_viewport();
--- a/source/shared.h
+++ b/source/shared.h
@@ -1283,6 +1283,10 @@ GLboolean change_stencil_config(SceGxmStencilOp *cfg, GLenum new_cfg); // Change
 GLboolean change_stencil_func_config(SceGxmStencilFunc *cfg, GLenum new_cfg); // Changes current in use stencil test function value
 void update_alpha_test_settings(void); // Changes current in use alpha test operation value
 void update_scissor_test(void); // Changes current in use scissor test region
+void vgl_mk_scene_begin(SceGxmDepthStencilSurface *ds); // 1.3 MASK_KEEP (patch 0026): a scene began on `ds` (NULL: none)
+void vgl_mk_forget(const void *surface); // 1.3 MASK_KEEP: new depth/stencil memory at `surface`
+void vgl_mk_touch(void); // 1.3 MASK_KEEP: the open scene's mask may have changed outside update_scissor_test
+extern GLboolean vgl_mask_keep;
 void reset_scissor_test_region(void); // Resets scissor test region to default values
